Hi,

> Is it a problem with es_CO.UTF-8 configuration and KDE or Qt or just rkward?

RKWard just uses the katepart (the embeddable version of the kwrite/kate editor)
for the script editor, and certainly does not implement any low-level editing
code like for composing accented characters. So I think the katepart (i.e. KDE
libraries) is to blame, here.

Note that RKWard 0.5.0 uses the KDE 4 libraries, and hence also katepart from
KDE 4. Most of your other KDE applications are probably still using KDE 3 versions,
which might explain why you see this bug in rkward, only.

